<title>TURKEY: Turk Kartonsan Q1 profits fall 10.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Kartonsan Q1 profits fall 10.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   467.90 vs   1,573.48</p>
<p>    Net profit		    758.01 vs     849.68</p>
<p>    Net sales		   2,225.08 vs   1,245.53</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    454.07 vs     423.46</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  843.22 vs     809.32</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	  99.06 vs	51.43</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   9.40 vs	 3.71</p>
<p>    Total debts		 4,823.07 vs   2,226.67</p>
<p>    Equity			6,928.80 vs   5,029.54</p>
<p>    Capital		     1,620.00 vs     540.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Kartonsan Karton Sanayi ve Ticaret A.S. is Turkey's leading white-lined chipboard and triplex board producer.</p>
<p>The company plans to further raise its capital to 2.025 trillion lira by issuing a 0.25 bonus for one existing share and to pay a 1,200 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from 1996 profits from May 21.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
